# Box-score CSVs are fetched fresh in CI on every run — they are build
# artifacts, not source. Keeping them out of git avoids bloating history
# (the play-by-play file is ~13 MB and would churn daily).
*.csv

# Reference / scratch files that don't belong in the deployable repo
*.xlsx
.Rhistory
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Private product/strategy docs — keep out of the public repo
COLUMN-REDESIGN.*
WNBA-STATS-EXPLORER.md
CLAUDE.md
Product Archive/

# Daily Bluesky engagement briefs (generated by the bluesky-brief skill) —
# personal working notes, not site source
bluesky-briefs/

# Work-in-progress prototypes — anything with "prototype" in the name
*prototype*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
wnba_linescores_2026.json

# Ephemeral payload for the Bluesky auto-post — regenerated every build
social_payload.json
